<title>USA: High pressure remains in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>High pressure remains in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, high pressure aloft over Brazil's coffee belt continues to appear strong enough to block any cold air currently in Argentina from moving into the region, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Partly to mostly cloudy skies were reported in main growing areas of the belt this morning. Temperatures have been in the 50's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>Dryness is expected throughout northern areas of the region through Monday. Occasional showers may hit southern portions of the belt. Low temperatures should remain in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>There is no damaging cold weather expected during the next seven days, WSC said.</p>
<p>((Eileen Houlihan, New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
